omtd:MorphologicalAnalysis a omtd:Operation,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Morphological analysis"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The analysis of the structure of words and their relations to other words as regards their form and derivation"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "General morphological analyisis"@en ;
    skos:broader omtd:LinguisticAnalysis ;
    skos:definition "The technologies for or the process of tracing the inflectional, derivational, and compounding processes in the formation of a given word in order to determine properties such as stem form, part-of-speech and inflectional information. As a crucial preprocessing step, morphological analysis is used in virtually all fields of natural language processing."@en ;
    skos:inScheme omtd:OperationScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "Morphological analysis"@en .

omtd:MultilingualGeneration a omtd:Operation,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Multilingual generation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The task/process of generating content in multiple languages"@en ;
    skos:broader omtd:NaturalLanguageGeneration ;
    skos:definition "Multilingual generation is the verbalization of a non-linguistic semantic representation in different human languages. The language of choice is usually a parameter to a multilingual generation system. A typical instance of multilingual generation is found in interlingual machine translation, when multiple target languages are involved. Other instances include report generation systems for multiple languages (such as Temsis-Gen) and grammar-based realizers (such as FUF/SURGE)."@en,
        "Multilingual generation is the verbalisation of a non-linguistic semantic representation in different human languages. The language of choice is usually a parameter to a multilingual generation system. A typical instance of multilingual generation is found in interlingual machine translation, when multiple target languages are involved. Other instances include report generation systems for multiple languages (such as Temsis-Gen) and grammar-based realisers (such as FUF/SURGE)."@en-gb ;
    skos:inScheme omtd:OperationScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "Multilingual generation"@en .

